meta {
  name: Resolve the topic to content
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curriculum-nodes/{{curriculumTopicId}}/content
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.curriculum_id: eq {{curriculumId}}
  res.body.count: eq 1
  res.body.resolution: eq unindexed
  res.body.content[0].placement_id: eq {{placementId}}
  res.body.content[0].exact: eq true
  res.body.content[0].page_start: eq 12
  res.body.content[0].retrieval_state: eq not_indexed
  res.body.counts.not_indexed: eq 1
  res.body.counts.unreadable: eq 0
}

docs {
  The question this whole surface is built to answer: a pupil asks about prime
  factorisation, and this turns that syllabus point into the pages that teach
  it.

  retrieval_state is not_indexed here, and that is the truth today rather than
  a defect. Indexing sits behind RETRIEVAL_INDEX_ENABLED, which is off, so
  publishing the textbook in folder 10 catalogued it and never sent it to the
  retrieval engine. Turn the flag on, publish, let the engine ingest, and the
  same request answers current. Do not read this assert as a bug report, and do
  not change it to current until the flag is on.

  The five states are separate answers on purpose, because the fix differs:

  not_indexed     mapped, published, never sent to the engine
  stale           indexed, but the asset has been replaced since
  current         indexed and the digest still matches
  unpublished     mapped, but the item is a draft, so nothing may read it
  source_deleted  the asset behind it is gone

  resolution is the same judgement for the node as a whole: resolved if
  anything is searchable, unindexed, unpublished or source_deleted if the only
  reason nothing is, unmapped if no placement exists at all, and restricted if
  placements exist but this caller may read none of the content behind them.
  restricted and unmapped are deliberately different: "there is nothing" and
  "there is something you may not see" are not the same answer, and a client
  that shows them the same way teaches pupils to stop asking.

  Only confirmed placements count by default. The whole-book placement from
  request 2 is still proposed, so it is not here.
}
